{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"agent_message","text":"The first run found one real mismatch: for `%d` text beyond the host `long` range, glibc saturates during conversion before narrowing to 32-bit, while Rust accumulated directly modulo 32 bits. That made `9223372036854775808` become `-1` in C but `0` in Rust, changing route validation; I’ll record it in `ERRORS.md` and adjust the parser to match the observed C conversion."}}
